      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree with some of this. It would be nice to have an overhaul of the current public world uploading system, but I can see how that isn't a priority.\nI don't agree with the idea of users having world mod status, or having user blacklists. From my perspective when you upload a public world you are giving any user the ability to make an instance of that world to do with as they please. Having a list of moderators or people you don't want to enter your world goes against that freedom and would restrict what people can do in their own instances.\nAlso a trusted creator content program already exists in the current beta. And I could see them limiting features only to people with higher trust levels such as trusted users and veterans in the future.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
