      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I do agree that users should have some sort of distinguishing feature for being a successful content creator, I completely disagree with having global mod status for your world.  It would only promote cliques even more and just lead to people getting randomly kicked because either A: The creator doesn't like them or B: They aren't in the creator's group.  I do love this suggestion though!  \n\nAs a content creator that has had their world previously reviewed and posted as public, it would be super nice to have the ability to update my world as I pleased.  Maybe mods could get a list of worlds that were uploaded that week and give a review every week instead of daily at the same time for each and every upload.  I think this would take a load off of staff as well because instead of reviewing the same worlds a few times in a week they would only be doing it once.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
