      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5bab44ebfb32cd1c27e87c90",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think a blacklist wouldn't be a great idea in many cases it could be abused for avatar worlds aka someone pinching someone elses avatar then popping it into the avatar world followed by them blacklisting the person they have stolen the avatar from. \nI think instead of the 24 hour limit between updating it should be a 24 hour grace period after updating to allow for bug fixes, this gives the content creator more time after it has been made public to fix bugs. \nI also think if you have more than one world you should be allowed to update all worlds at the same time. It means that as the creator of the world you aren't spending time waiting.\nInstead of a rank system I think a small addition such as a badge to say you've created content for the game would suffice. I think worlds popularity shouldn't matter with this, because there are plenty of worlds out there that a very impressive that just dont get the popularity even though they are more of a professional standard (looking at things like the ghibili world that just don't get the numbers) Thats not to say all content creators don't put effort in everyone has their own skill levels at the end of the day. I just think if you are going to implement it it shouldn't be based on the worlds popularity more so on how that world has been developed and the level of quality. \n\nThis is just my two cents into this however some may not like how I think about it. I just think it would pull people away from eachother and idolise certain people which for a social game like this with a <6k co current players at this point in time is not healthy.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
