  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-26T08:35:55.647Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hey VRchat, \n\nWith the new upcoming ranking system, it feels like there is a gap for a very important and active part of the VRchat community, and that is content creators.\n\nPeople who publish public worlds and avatars provide the very content which provides settings for users to be entertained, and avatars with which users to express themselves.\n\nWhile there is the curated spotlight list, and what seems to be the rarely-updated \"popular\" list, I know of many content creators (myself obviously included) who are frustrated by the lack of communication with developers and community managers in terms of content creation policies and upcoming updates to VRchat.\n\nIt would be nice, especially for those of us with very active public worlds who have proven we create consistent, quality content, and abide by VRchat's rules, to be able to have access to more tools to keep our worlds secure.\n\nFor instance.  Having the ability to grant users we trust \"mod\" status in our worlds so they can kick / mute people as necessary.  Creating user black lists to prevent cancer groups from bothering other people using our worlds.  The list goes on and on.\n\nLastly, as a verified, trusted, content creator, it'd be nice to finally be free of the weekly / monthly cycle of having to have our worlds continually re-verified whenever we need to make an update, or do bug fixes with our worlds.  There have been too many times where after waiting a day for the world to be re-verified for public use, a bug we missed has to bring the world down for yet another day until it can be once again verified.\n\nI understand that a lot of these features require a reworking of VRchat systems, or aren't a high priority, but I'll hope you'll consider at the very least implementing a verified / trusted content creator program in the future as I believe it would definitely speed up the evolution and amount of quality content made available to VRchat as a whole.\n\nsincerely, \nLittle Mouse of [ subcom ] avatars",
